#!/bin/sh
# ubus object "luci.cfst" backing the LuCI JS views. Standard rpcd sh
# dispatcher: `list` enumerates methods, `call <method>` reads a JSON
# object on stdin and must print a JSON object on stdout.

. /usr/share/libubox/jshn.sh
. /usr/share/cfst/backend-common.sh

read_input() {
	local input
	input="$(cat)"
	[ -n "$input" ] || input='{}'
	json_load "$input"
}

resolve_target_backend() {
	# $1 = optional explicit backend override from the caller
	local explicit="$1" cfg
	if [ -n "$explicit" ]; then
		resolve_backend "$explicit"
		return
	fi
	cfg=$(uci -q get cfst.global.backend)
	resolve_backend "${cfg:-auto}"
}

handle_detect_backends() {
	local b resolved hint
	json_init
	json_add_array available
	for b in passwall2 passwall openclash; do
		backend_available "$b" && json_add_string "" "$b"
	done
	json_close_array
	hint=$(resolve_target_backend "" 2>/dev/null)
	json_add_string active_hint "$hint"
	json_dump
}

handle_list_nodes() {
	local backend_arg resolved tsv id remark address type

	read_input
	json_get_var backend_arg backend 2>/dev/null

	resolved=$(resolve_target_backend "$backend_arg" 2>/dev/null)
	if [ -z "$resolved" ]; then
		json_init
		json_add_boolean ok 0
		json_add_string error "no single backend resolved (none or multiple detected)"
		json_add_array nodes
		json_close_array
		json_dump
		return
	fi

	source_backend "$resolved"
	tsv=$(list_nodes 2>/dev/null)

	json_init
	json_add_boolean ok 1
	json_add_string backend "$resolved"
	json_add_array nodes
	while IFS="$(printf '\t')" read -r id remark address type || [ -n "$id" ]; do
		[ -n "$id" ] || continue
		json_add_object ""
		json_add_string id "$id"
		json_add_string remark "$remark"
		json_add_string address "$address"
		json_add_string type "$type"
		json_close_object
	done <<-CFST_LN
	$tsv
	CFST_LN
	json_close_array
	json_dump
}

handle_get_arch() {
	local arch installed mtime
	arch=$(detect_arch)
	if [ -x "$CFST_BIN" ]; then
		installed=1
		mtime=$(date -r "$CFST_BIN" +%s 2>/dev/null)
		[ -n "$mtime" ] || mtime=0
	else
		installed=0
		mtime=0
	fi
	json_init
	json_add_string arch "$arch"
	json_add_boolean installed "$installed"
	json_add_int mtime "$mtime"
	json_dump
}

handle_download_binary() {
	local mirror
	read_input
	json_get_var mirror mirror_prefix 2>/dev/null

	if pid_file_alive "$DOWNLOAD_PID_FILE"; then
		json_init
		json_add_boolean started 0
		json_add_string error "download already in progress"
		json_dump
		return
	fi

	( /usr/share/cfst/download-cfst.sh "$mirror" >/dev/null 2>&1 & )

	json_init
	json_add_boolean started 1
	json_dump
}

handle_download_status() {
	if [ -f "$DOWNLOAD_STATUS_FILE" ]; then
		cat "$DOWNLOAD_STATUS_FILE"
	else
		echo '{"state":"idle","time":0,"arch":"","message":""}'
	fi
}

handle_run_now() {
	if pid_file_alive "$PID_FILE"; then
		json_init
		json_add_boolean started 0
		json_add_string error "a run is already in progress"
		json_dump
		return
	fi

	( /usr/bin/cfst-run >/dev/null 2>&1 & )

	json_init
	json_add_boolean started 1
	json_dump
}

handle_run_status() {
	if [ -f "$RUN_STATUS_FILE" ]; then
		cat "$RUN_STATUS_FILE"
	else
		echo '{"running":false,"backend":"","last_run":0,"last_result":"","last_ip":""}'
	fi
}

handle_get_log() {
	local lines content

	read_input
	json_get_var lines lines 2>/dev/null
	[ -n "$lines" ] || lines=200

	content=$(tail -n "$lines" "$LOG_FILE" 2>/dev/null)

	json_init
	json_add_array lines
	while IFS= read -r line || [ -n "$line" ]; do
		json_add_string "" "$line"
	done <<-CFST_LOG
	$content
	CFST_LOG
	json_close_array
	json_dump
}

handle_clear_log() {
	: > "$LOG_FILE"
	json_init
	json_add_boolean ok 1
	json_dump
}

handle_get_results() {
	local rows c1 c2 c3 c4 c5 c6 c7

	if [ ! -f "$RESULT_CSV" ]; then
		json_init
		json_add_array results
		json_close_array
		json_dump
		return
	fi

	rows=$(tail -n +2 "$RESULT_CSV" 2>/dev/null)

	json_init
	json_add_array results
	while IFS=',' read -r c1 c2 c3 c4 c5 c6 c7 || [ -n "$c1" ]; do
		[ -n "$c1" ] || continue
		if [ -z "$c6" ]; then
			json_add_object ""
			json_add_boolean raw 1
			json_add_string line "$c1,$c2,$c3,$c4,$c5,$c6,$c7"
			json_close_object
		else
			json_add_object ""
			json_add_string ip "$c1"
			json_add_string sent "$c2"
			json_add_string received "$c3"
			json_add_string loss "$c4"
			json_add_string latency "$c5"
			json_add_string speed "$c6"
			json_add_string colo "$c7"
			json_close_object
		fi
	done <<-CFST_RES
	$rows
	CFST_RES
	json_close_array
	json_dump
}

case "$1" in
	list)
		json_init
		json_add_object "list_nodes";      json_add_string backend ""; json_close_object
		json_add_object "detect_backends"; json_close_object
		json_add_object "get_arch";        json_close_object
		json_add_object "download_binary"; json_add_string mirror_prefix ""; json_close_object
		json_add_object "download_status"; json_close_object
		json_add_object "run_now";         json_close_object
		json_add_object "run_status";      json_close_object
		json_add_object "get_log";         json_add_int lines 0; json_close_object
		json_add_object "clear_log";       json_close_object
		json_add_object "get_results";     json_close_object
		json_dump
		;;
	call)
		case "$2" in
			list_nodes)       handle_list_nodes ;;
			detect_backends)  handle_detect_backends ;;
			get_arch)         handle_get_arch ;;
			download_binary)  handle_download_binary ;;
			download_status)  handle_download_status ;;
			run_now)          handle_run_now ;;
			run_status)       handle_run_status ;;
			get_log)          handle_get_log ;;
			clear_log)        handle_clear_log ;;
			get_results)      handle_get_results ;;
			*) echo '{}'; exit 1 ;;
		esac
		;;
esac
